Sure! If you already have your array of objects (let’s call it `myItemList`), you can use the `prioritizeAndSort` helper like this:

```javascript
// Assuming myItemList looks something like this:
const myItemList = [
  { name: 'Alpha', status: 'normal' },
  { name: 'Bravo', status: 'urgent' },
  { name: 'Charlie', status: 'normal' },
  { name: 'Delta', status: 'urgent' }
];

// Call the helper to get the sorted result
const sortedResult = prioritizeAndSort({
  items: JSON.stringify(myItemList),
  priorityStatus: 'urgent',
  ascending: true
});

console.log(sortedResult);
```

If you want me to run this for you, just paste your actual array into `myItemList` above and let me know!
